## 8. MCP Integration

This framework includes an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that enables AI-assisted test automation workflows.

### Capabilities

The MCP server provides tools for:
- Generating test scenarios from user stories
- Discovering page elements for automation
- Generating Page Objects, Tasks, and Roles
- Creating test runners from BDD scenarios
- Running tests and analyzing failures
- Tracking test coverage

### Usage

The MCP integration follows the same 4-layer architecture patterns documented above. AI-generated code adheres to all framework conventions including:
- Proper layer separation
- Correct decorator usage
- State-check methods for assertions
- No return values from Tasks/Roles

For detailed MCP workflow documentation and integration guides, please contact the repository maintainer.

